.TH "DOCUMENT.HIDDEN" "3JS" "July 3, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Document.hidden \- Document: hidden property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]Document.hidden\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property returns a
Boolean value indicating if the page is considered hidden or not.
This can be used to check whether the document is in the background or
in a minimized window, or is otherwise not visible to the user.
.PP
The \f[CR]Document.visibilityState\f[R] property provides an alternative
way to determine whether the page is hidden.
.SH VALUE
A Boolean value, \f[CR]true\f[R] if the page is hidden, and
\f[CR]false\f[R] otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
document.addEventListener(\(dqvisibilitychange\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(document.hidden);
  \f[I]// Modify behavior\&...\f[R]
});
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Document.visibilityState\f[R]
